  body = "Retain the complete Crucible integration on the sole pinned QEMU base.\nSupply required run and teardown rows with real compiled fixture layouts\nand same-module exported C component providers. Derive modeled allowance\nfrom the genuine backing planner and retain the original 1 MiB refusal.\nAssert exact issued claims, retained roster/worker charges and task plans,\nwhile preserving required-role omissions and every cleanup behavior.\n\nAdmit the actual source-built glibc 2.39 cohort after auditing its GNU\nrelease allocator, TLS and user-stack thread paths. Keep the existing\n2.42 cohort and every loader, allocator, environment and THP refusal.\nThe unchanged bound covers 32 KiB heap/header minimum, 128 KiB top-pad,\n1 MiB morecore fallback, backing-page rounding, actual control requests,\nDTV max-module-id plus 14 surplus and two headers, tcache (64 bins under\n2.39, bounded by 76), and each loaded TLS size plus alignment. Explicit\nuser stacks contain pthread/first TSD/static TLS and bypass stack caches;\nfirst-thread signal setup allocates nothing. Refuse changed environment\ninputs and invalid stacks without charge or birth. Task/TLS accounting\ndoes not prove physical libc backing return.\n\nRepair serialized component dependency closures with literal native helper\nbodies and configured genuine QOM support/linker objects. Keep bounded\ncomponent providers separate from that linked support and preserve original\ncompiler target options. Retain the genuine linked RCU worker after its\nactual callback drain, including its native registry and task census;\nnever erase or relabel the record. Refresh exact input fingerprints.\n\nPreserve configured healthy completion with actual C Bridge/Child placement,\nregistration holder transfer, bounded RUN/teardown task enrollment and entry,\nRUN socket handoff, semaphore lifetime, close/join/control destruction and\nstack/Bridge/Child storage return. Bound join observations by the same\nretained installing and containing deadlines, without renewing admission.\nKeep exact residual history charged. Reach the unavailable-runtime negative\nthrough actual controller reservation before its disclosed scratch input.\nPrepared-family and completion enrollment remain isolated modeled inputs;\nno worker born, ready or returned flag is seeded. These component lifetimes\nqualify no standing, entered Original, production Rust module, Source/CPU\nactivation or launched lifecycle/VM behavior. The mandatory launched capture\nlifecycle refusal remains unchanged.\n\nRetain a completed actual command-reader journal in one paid inline delivery\nowner, including born-negative output. Pin the real receive/member/lender,\nauthenticate thread/process and nonwrapping serials, and retain the exact\noriginal creation output before canonical Runtime transfer. Refuse copied\ncreation/use holders, stale serials, saturation and reissue from the same\nstill-retained receive. Local same-thread uses pin only this lifetime; the\nsingle paid use slot admits no worker, nested or multi-vCPU cohort. Identity\nand use returns consume only on zero under the registry mutex and preserve\nall holders on every negative. Returning local delivery leaves the received\nrequest, module payload epoch and publisher/peer obligations retained.\n\nExercise literal receive/delivery bodies with an actual registered C reader,\nreal mutex/thread/process/runtime storage, and explicit modeled member and\nstanding boundary inputs. These component controls issue no action Original,\nmodule payload ownership, ACK, ActionReturn, Source/CPU activation or launched\nlifecycle qualification. Preserve the mandatory launched-lifecycle refusal.\n\nFirst-bind module payload claim/release with member v3 to the genuine retained\ncomplete child. Keep v2 explicitly payload-unavailable. Journal the exact paid\nSource field, module-local serial and real transition before the masked callback\noutside Source's mutex. Retain every born pair and uncertainty independently of\ncallback status and physical post; refuse local identity return with actual\npayload, borrowers or transition debt. No standing/Original query is inferred.\nSave genuine release destruction/nulling before independent post so a negative\npost cannot resurrect payload debt. Preserve the first release diagnostic even\nwhen a later actual retry consumes; pure local return independently records the\nclosed delivery lifetime. Parent receive and publisher/peer obligations remain.\n\nExercise literal v3 construction/transfer with a real C reader-deposited child\njournal, exact canonical claim and destruction, actual journal-lock borrowers,\nborn-negative custody, half-pair/duplicate binding refusals, copied field/serial\nrefusals, reentrant transition exclusion, partial/contradictory output retention,\nand consumed-before-negative-post cleanup. Installation and standing inputs are\nexplicitly modeled; this is no production Rust child, operational payload use,\naction Original, ACK, ActionReturn, Source activation or VM qualification.\n\nNominate each actual received journal at birth inside Source's authenticated\nReady factual callback. Claim completion alone may retain its exact canonical\nmodule payload field/local serial, first-bound child/member and standing lender\nin a paid Source handoff. The actual execution carrier retains the exact Source\ninterior before independent post and normal observation return; this physical\npin survives Ready exit without extending or reusing its entered marker.\nPreserve born-negative custody and block actual payload, delivery and execution\nreturn until dependencies close. No copied facts or caller tuple creates it.\n\nProvide factual ready_return consumption independently from signed status.\nAuthenticate the real delivery, exact execution holder and actual local uses;\nrecord real consumption before independent post. Missing physical consumption\nbecomes uncertain refusal, never output success. Absence/completed return is\nterminal for that delivery and preserves the first return error across retry.\nExercise literal Source/coordinator dispatch and holder-return bodies with\nexplicitly modeled installation, standing and Main-loop entry inputs, keeping\nall earlier controls. Ready retention alone supplies no CPU operation use,\naction Original, Source activation, ACK, ActionReturn or launched qualification.\n\nAt the actual Main control boundary retain its genuine CONTROL descriptor/group\nuse and QOM CPU reference with the Source allocation receipt and generation.\nAuthenticate the exact installed core dispatch field, thread/process and real\nCPU roster before publishing a distinct factual Native frame. Before independent\npost retain an exact paid Source borrower of the Ready handoff, canonical module\npayload field, first-bound child/member and standing lender. Neither copied\nholders nor first_cpu equality issues this loan or CPU operation permission.\n\nKeep the Main invocation/return journal separate from Stop admission. Preserve\nborn-negative outputs; block Ready, payload and delivery cleanup while a real\nMain borrower remains. Close actual QOM and Native descriptor dependencies before\nconsuming the Source holder and independently checking post. Retain uncertain\ntransitions, and never resurrect physical custody after a negative post. Actual\nnested masks prevent return; real QOM finalizers run while the descriptor/frame\nand Source borrower remain pinned. Keep fixed pools and all existing limits.\n\nExercise literal Core dispatch, Native registry and Source borrower bodies with\nreal mutex/thread/process identity, QOM reference/finalizer execution and actual\nnested mask return. Installed publication, allocator observation, Main/BQL entry\nand a minimal CPU class remain explicitly modeled component inputs. Preserve all\nearlier scenarios and causal controls. This physical custody cut grants no CPU\noperation, entered action Original, publisher membership, activation, ACK,\nActionReturn, peer return or launched lifecycle/VM qualification.\n\nFirst-bind v4 member callbacks for one prepaid nominal module-payload lifetime\nborrow under the exact Main owner. Authenticate the canonical payload field and\nlocal serial through the retained child journal. Keep older member editions\nexplicitly borrow-unavailable, and refuse half-pairs before member birth.\n\nJournal invocation before the masked callback, keeping exact stable holder and\nserial output fields. Accept known absence only from a genuine empty NULL/0\nnegative refusal; retain unknown or contradictory outputs. Preserve born-negative\nrecords and independent acquire/status/post facts. Release authenticates the\nactual born token and original serial, clears both original output fields, and\nrecords real consumption before independent callback status and Source post.\nNeither a scalar output nor a copied field can close the physical dependency.\n\nThe actual Core Main exit attempts module return before QOM, Native descriptor\nand Source borrower return. Unknown or unconsumed module debt retains those exact\nowners and the Ready handoff, blocks parent teardown and subsequent dispatch,\nand ends the real entered marker. No stale Main phase authorizes later retry;\na genuine cleanup entry producer remains required for that terminal containment.\n\nExercise literal Native/Source/Core consumers with a modeled module journal,\nexplicitly modeled installed publication/allocation/Main entry inputs, genuine\nmutex/process/thread identity, exact field custody and independent post errors.\nPreserve existing scenarios and limits. Local opaque lifetime borrowing exports\nno payload reference, action/class, entered Original, publisher membership, CPU\noperation permission, activation, ACK, ActionReturn or physical peer return.\nIt does not qualify the actual module/QEMU pairing or launched lifecycle.\n\nRequire CRUCSRV4/schema4 standing records with big-endian producer-retention\nedition1 at offset196. Preserve the 1496/1504/1520 publication extents and\nprocess-purpose8 envelope. Bind the declaration in the sealed initial record,\nrequire it on subsequent observations and reject every predecessor, zero and\nunknown edition before producing output. Rename every actual decoder caller,\nincluding the preinit literal closure, and refresh exact fixture fingerprints.\n\nDocument the producer promise: every born row, including dirty/unprojected\nrows, stays retained; exposed matching actions are irrevocably pending before\nrequest publication and cannot race unpublished abandonment. Exact action birth\ncannot be replaced until authenticated assigned-peer local closure. Local\nsubscriber closure never retires publisher-owned rows, and producer death or\nunknown cleanup does not certify physical return. This compatibility cut does\nnot yet construct a Source subscription or issue operation/action authority.\n\nExercise current syntax plus predecessor, edition, byte-order and unchanged\noutput refusals. Retain prior native causal timeout and launched lifecycle\nfailures as unresolved observations; no decoder or component result qualifies\nactivation, Original, publisher membership, ACK or ActionReturn.\n\nComplete the lifetime component's real constructor-RCU prerequisite before its\nforeign-process identity control forks. A child otherwise can restart RCU while\ninheriting the thread-registry mutex held by the vanished constructor helper.\nDrain actual RCU callbacks, then inspect the real registry under that mutex:\nexactly one retained RCU_RESTART helper, its coordinator, no overflow and no\nin-flight starts. Expose the actual starts counter in process-private inventory\nonly. Keep the helper record alive, every process-refusal assertion and all\nexisting build/test ceilings. No sleep, synthetic readiness or fork grant is\nsubstituted. Refresh exact extractor fingerprints after the native header edit.\n\nThe fixture starts no other QEMU threads in this scenario; actual callback\ncompletion follows thread registration, start-end consumption and RCU reader\nregistration. This closes a concrete inherited-lock race, not the production\nhot-fork admission contract. Independently rebuilt retained-start debt refuses\nbefore fork. Preserve failed prior causal attempts and the mandatory launched\nSource/Root lifecycle refusal until their respective fresh checks qualify.\n\n\nCapture a nominal publisher subscription only from the actual outside-BQL Ready\nhandoff, completed matching receive, canonical payload, first-bound member,\nassigned mapping and installed schema-4 retention promise. Require its complete\nborn/projected Running cohort and retain the exact sequence before independent\npost. Main action children borrow that owner; decoded equality cannot issue it.\nSingle sequence-current drift refusal avoids coherent standing reads under BQL.\n\nSeparate local view closure from a prepaid terminal writer. Close actual Main,\nsemantic and Ready children, then physically destroy the canonical module\npayload before publishing local closure. Retain delivery/member/mapping/lender\nthrough uncertainty. Observe but never clear the Host birth hold. Publish the\n184-byte CRUCRET1 record with checked nonwrapping atomic sequence CAS/stores/CAS,\nsaving real final-CAS consumption before independent post. Preserve first/post\nfailures separately; issue no progress witness or publisher row retirement.\n\nFirst-bind member v5 semantic enter/current/post/return to its retained complete\nchild. Construct the actual Source action only inside the genuine entered Main\ncallback route, with its nominal subscriber and canonical v4 payload borrower.\nKeep raw callback/post outcomes separate from born token and physical return.\nAuthenticate actual Main/Native frames, semantic evidence and immutable row\nlimits, including an independent containing Preparation row. Actual async\nmaterial retains that same action and frozen limits after callback exit; later\nphysical cleanup cannot revive CALLING. Close semantic action before v4 payload,\nQOM/CPU, Source Main and descriptor return. Final module evidence precedes exact\ncanonical consumption; save consumption before independently refusing an\nincomplete healthy return. Legacy member editions remain semantic-unavailable.\n\nComponent controls exercise literal custody and writer bodies with real C\npayload journals, QOM retention and writable atomic mapping. Standing/assigned\ninstallation and local semantic boundary inputs are explicitly modeled; these\ncontrols do not qualify the installed Rust semantic path or launched lifecycle.\nRetain every original scenario, resource ceiling and refusal. Independently\nrebuilt publisher and literal evidence defects must fail their causal assertions.\nAdd five explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later files and retain all existing file licenses.\nKeep prior failed causal attempts and mandatory launched lifecycle refusal\nvisible; no operation/activation or peer-return qualification follows from\ncompilation or modeled component success.\n\n\nInclude the newly referenced actual Core Main/action predicates and their real\ninactive journal declarations in the owning Source/Native extractor closure.\nNo fixture may replace those predicates with successful authority providers.\nPreserve the first incomplete-closure link failure as a failed build attempt.\n\nRetain selected initial CPU callbacks under the actual stopped construction\nOriginal. Defer enqueue until each actual Source allocation receipt exists,\nretain its canonical QOM participant and registration group, and complete the\nreal CPU FIFO callback/barrier before construction Post. Authenticate distinct\ncallback entry, return and final physical consumption; pre-enqueue refusal\ncloses only the actual unentered child. Check actual roster generation after\nQOM unref before advancing its iterator. No FIFO marker invents callback return.\n\nGuard selected realized capability, manifest, bind, seal and register-list SDK\nfactories with the actual class-0 child and exact Core/Native callback. Preserve\nindependent first/post failures. Their missing bounded native constructor payer\nstill refuses before factory allocation with ENOKEY; unselected paths keep their\nexisting behavior. Generic VCPU_INIT remains factual and inactive; no new\nworkspace, operation, activation, ACK or physical peer-return permission exists.\n\nCharge the actual Core initial-dispatch static extent and enlarged actual CPU\nallocation owner through their existing paid layouts. Extract the real storage\nand getter for component sizing, retaining exact source and dependency guards.\nAdd two explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later includes. Literal clock and SDK-history tests\nexercise independent total/progress/clock and signed-history omission controls.\nThe assertion-only actual initial callback hooks remain unexecuted pending the\ngenuine installed-module launch harness; compilation and pure predicate tests\ncannot qualify that route. Preserve original ceilings, all previous failed\nattempts and mandatory launched Source/Root lifecycle refusal.\n\nReplace the hardware manifest and binding GArrays with the actual bounded\nsix-row/six-binding typed declaration. Preserve ordinary architecture branches,\nordering and binding behavior; refuse sticky overflow before publication.\nCharge the entire declaration once through its genuine installation floor,\nincluding its inactive lease and terminal journals, for the image lifetime.\n\nRetain the private paired hardware constructor lease under the actual initial\nCPU child, QOM allocation receipts, fixed account and construction Original.\nKeep actual Native issuing/holder predicates and post-ATEXIT process/thread\nscope distinct from installation or callback facts. Terminal return requires\nreal registry retirement and worker, material, action, Main, Ready, Park and\ninitial-CPU closure, plus no registered handlers, staged VMState or pending events.\nConsume logical lease dependencies only after unpublication; static image\nbacking remains charged. Selected public SDK and internal lazy builders remain\nprebirth-refused. These inactive seams do not qualify an accepted constructor,\nexecuted callback, operation, activation or physical peer return.\n\nRefuse selected register and interrupt lazy factories before CPU lookup or\ncached-row reuse, retaining unselected preconditions and behavior. Extract the\nactual typed catalogue declaration/getter and enlarged Core dispatch journal\nfor component sizing; retain exact source/dependency fingerprints. Run literal\nstorage/branch, selected refusal and physical-debt controls with independent\nomission mutations, and document actual installed-runner/factory prerequisites.\nAdd two explicitly GPL-2.0-or-later focused tests and preserve every existing\nfile license, assertion and resource limit. Initial callback and lease assertion\nhooks remain unexecuted; retain all prior failed attempts and the mandatory\nlaunched Source/Root lifecycle refusal.";
